    <h1 class="title">Systems I've built</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A working demo you can open right in the browser, and a few smaller apps you can
      download and run yourself. Source and setup notes are linked with each one.
    </p>

    <div class="dossier">
      <article class="dossier__entry">
        <span class="dossier__numeral">i.</span>
        <h3>Mock Payroll System</h3>
        <p>
          A self-contained payroll web app — employee records, hours, deductions, and
          payslip generation — built to practice full end-to-end system design rather
          than a single tutorial feature.
        </p>
        <p class="dossier__stack">Node.js — Express — EJS — SQLite</p>
        <div class="dossier__actions">
          <!-- Opens the running app in a new tab. Point this at wherever the
               payroll app is actually deployed, or leave it on /payroll to
               use the built-in stub route. -->
          <a href="/payroll" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--primary">
            Open live demo
          </a>
          <a href="#" class="btn btn--ghost">View source</a>
        </div>
        <div class="dossier__plate">
          <div class="plate">
            <div class="plate__placeholder">Screenshot — payroll dashboard</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="dossier__entry">
        <span class="dossier__numeral">ii.</span>
        <h3>Project name</h3>
        <p>One or two sentences on what this app does and the problem it solves.</p>
        <p class="dossier__stack">Tech — Tech — Tech</p>
        <div class="dossier__actions">
